{"id": "unknown-2026-07-17-011", "date": "2026-07-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["trade_tariff", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Giving away excess daytime solar for free", "content": "<p>Australia is turning excess midday solar into a consumer benefit through free “solar sharer” electricity tariffs, enabling households to shift loads, charge batteries and EVs, and cut energy bills dramatically. With rooftop solar, storage, electrification, and smarter tariffs, Australia is showing how market innovation can integrate large amounts of renewable energy at low cost.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/17/giving-away-excess-daytime-solar-for-free/\">Giving ", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/17/giving-away-excess-daytime-solar-for-free/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-17-012", "date": "2026-07-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Oman plans 6 GW solar cell, module factory", "content": "<p>Oman is investing in a 6 GW solar cell and module factory as part of a $1.74 billion investment package across 105 strategic projects.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/17/oman-plans-6-gw-solar-cell-module-factory/\">Oman plans 6 GW solar cell, module factory</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com\">pv magazine Global</a>.</p>\n", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/17/oman-plans-6-gw-solar-cell-module-factory/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-17-013", "date": "2026-07-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The Hydrogen Stream: Tanaka energizes 500 kW fuel cell facility in Japan", "content": "<p>In other news, John Cockerill Hydrogen unveiled France’s first 5 MW electrolyzer stack, while D3 Energy reported certified hydrogen and helium resources in Australia’s Arckaringa Basin with hydrogen concentrations of up to 11.5%. PowerCell, ECL, Air Liquide, and OMV announced new hydrogen projects spanning fuel cells for AI data centers, low-carbon hydrogen production, and a 140 MW electrolyzer facility, while researchers developed a low-temperature process to produce high-purity hydrogen fro", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/17/the-hydrogen-stream-tanaka-energizes-500-kw-pure-hydrogen-fuel-cell-facility-in-japan/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-17-014", "date": "2026-07-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["installation_demand", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "AI-powered 9-ton tracked robot for large-scale PV construction", "content": "<p>China-based Relu Robotics has developed a 9-ton robot that reportedly delivers accurate module handling and installation. The company says its tracked chassis, extended-range power system, and all-terrain capability enable operation across deserts, sand, wastelands, hills, and slopes under extreme conditions.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/17/ai-powered-9-ton-tracked-robot-for-large-scale-pv-construction/\">AI-powered 9-ton tracked robot for large-scale PV constru", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/17/ai-powered-9-ton-tracked-robot-for-large-scale-pv-construction/", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-07-17-015", "date": "2026-07-17", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 7, "week": 29, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Argentina’s electricity demand fell by 1,700 MW during World Cup semifinal against England", "content": "<p>Argentina’s World Cup semifinal against England triggered electricity demand fluctuations of up to 1,700 MW, according to CAMMESA. The grid operator said the main challenge was managing rapid changes in consumption, including a 1,500 MW rebound after the final whistle.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/17/argentinas-electricity-demand-fell-by-1700-mw-during-world-cup-semifinal-against-england/\">Argentina’s electricity demand fell by 1,700 MW during World Cup semifin", "sources": [{"name": "pv_magazine", "url": "https://www.pv-magazine.com/2026/07/17/argentinas-electricity-demand-fell-by-1700-mw-during-world-cup-semifinal-against-england/", "type": "rss"}]}
